## Q1: How do you use AI in your day-to-day job?

**Situation:** In my day-to-day role, I manage a .NET application deployed through Azure DevOps pipelines to an IIS-hosted Windows VM, with Cloudflare as the front door. A lot of my time used to go into manually checking pipeline logs, IIS logs, and monitoring dashboards to catch issues early.

**Task:** I wanted to reduce the manual effort in my daily routine and catch problems faster, without waiting for something to break first.

**Action:** I use AI tools daily in a few ways — asking an LLM to help write or review PowerShell/YAML scripts for pipeline tasks, using AI to summarize long pipeline logs so I don’t have to scroll through everything, and using AI-assisted monitoring to flag unusual patterns in traffic or errors before they become incidents. I also use AI to help draft documentation and runbooks after resolving issues, so the next person has context.

**Result:** This saves me a meaningful chunk of time every day, reduces repetitive manual log-checking, and means issues get caught and documented faster. It’s become a normal part of how I work, not a separate task.

