## Q2: How would you use AI agents in a DevOps workflow?

**Situation:** I deploy a .NET application through Azure DevOps pipelines to an IIS-hosted Windows VM, with Cloudflare in front as the front door. When a deployment failed or an app pool crashed, engineers had to manually go through pipeline logs and IIS Event Viewer to find out why.

**Task:** I needed a faster way to find the root cause without everyone digging through logs by hand.

**Action:** I added an AI agent to the pipeline. After a failed deployment, it automatically reads the pipeline logs and IIS logs, checks them against recent code changes, and posts a summary with the likely cause to our Teams channel.

**Result:** Diagnosis time dropped a lot. Junior engineers could fix common issues on their own without escalating, so senior engineers had more time for harder problems.

